      "writtenOn": "2024-01-29T22:10:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the tests assume that we start out in a state where `FP_CAPTURE_TYPE(response.mode)` is not `FP_CAPTURE_SIMPLE_IMAGE`. Is it possible to add a `zassert` here to verify that in order to prevent someone from accidentally changing these defaults in a way that would make the test pass even if switching to `FP_CAPTURE_SIMPLE_IMAGE` didn\u0027t actually work? (i.e., it was already initialized to that state.)\n\nI guess another way would be to add a helper function that you call at the beginning of each test that does the check.\n\nI don\u0027t think that either is required; just trying to see what is possible.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 337,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 349,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "8e9f2f94a1e3a112b9f45b73db9bfd6a669a4923",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
